---
import PostLayout from "~/layouts/PostLayout.astro";
---

<PostLayout
  title="Typography & layout test post"
  description="A hard-coded sample post used to validate the prose-blog styles, dark mode and reading layout end-to-end. Code-highlighting will be validated on real MDX posts after Phase 2."
  date={new Date("2026-05-10")}
  tags={["typography", "test", "astro"]}
  series="GNU/Linux Environment for Developers"
  readingTimeMinutes={4}
  cover_image="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1517694712202-14dd9538aa97?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1600&q=80"
>
  <p>
    This page exists to verify the <strong>typography pass</strong> of the modern dev blog look. It
    is not a real post — it will be deleted before the cutover. If headings, prose, lists, links,
    blockquotes and code blocks all read well in both light and dark mode, Phase 1 is done.
  </p>

  <h2>Headings should feel solid but not loud</h2>
  <p>
    Body text uses <code>Inter</code> at <code>1.0625rem</code> with <code>line-height: 1.75</code>.
    Display headings switch to <code>Lexend</code> with tight letter-spacing. The accent color is
    the existing brand green <code>#00ab6b</code>, lightened in dark mode for contrast.
  </p>

  <h3>Lists, links and emphasis</h3>
  <p>
    Inline links like <a href="https://astro.build">astro.build</a> are accent-colored. Lists are
    spaced for breathing room:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Sticky header with backdrop blur</li>
    <li>Sticky right-rail TOC (lands in Phase 4)</li>
    <li>Reading-progress bar at the top of post pages (Phase 4)</li>
    <li>⌘K palette wired to Pagefind (Phase 4)</li>
  </ul>

  <blockquote>
    <p>
      "The web is supposed to be fast." — every dev blog redesign post, ever. This one will
      actually try to be.
    </p>
  </blockquote>

  <h3>Code blocks (will use Expressive Code in real MDX posts)</h3>
  <p>This is a placeholder pre block — real code highlighting kicks in when posts are migrated to MDX in Phase 2:</p>

  <pre><code>{`import { defineCollection, z } from "astro:content";

const posts = defineCollection({
  schema: z.object({
    title: z.string(),
    description: z.string().optional(),
    date: z.coerce.date(),
    tags: z.array(z.string()).default([]),
  }),
});`}</code></pre>

  <h3>Tables</h3>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr><th>Phase</th><th>Status</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>1 — Skeleton</td><td>in progress</td></tr>
      <tr><td>2 — Content port</td><td>queued</td></tr>
      <tr><td>3 — Pages & homepage</td><td>queued</td></tr>
      <tr><td>4 — Polish</td><td>queued</td></tr>
      <tr><td>5 — Cutover</td><td>queued</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <hr />

  <p>If this page renders cleanly in both themes, Phase 1 ships.</p>
</PostLayout>
